<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Assistants</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
    Connect your AI assistant and it can read your training and write it: plan a block,
    log a session, correct a set you typed wrong. It sees your account and nothing else.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Connect one</h2>
  <%# The one-click box /docs has had since #359, here too since #637. /start and settings both
      send a signed-in lifter to this page, so somebody who signed up first and connected second
      -- the order /start suggests -- never saw the fastest way in and got the copy-and-paste one
      instead. Only where the deployment knows its own address, which the link is built from. %>
  <%- if @resource_url %>
    <div class="mt-3 rounded-xl border border-sky-200 bg-sky-50 p-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700">
        Using Claude? This opens its add-connector dialog with the address already filled in.
      </p>
      <a href="<%= claude_connector_url %>" rel="noopener"
         class="<%= button_style %> mt-3 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center bg-sky-800 px-4 text-sm
                font-semibold text-white hover:bg-sky-900">Add to Claude</a>
    </div>
  <%- end %>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-600">
    Any other assistant: add a custom connector and give it this address. It will send you
    back here to sign in and approve it, and once you have, it appears under Connected below.
  </p>
  <%- if @resource_url %>
    <div class="mt-3 flex items-center gap-2">
      <%# The copy button trims, so the whitespace this wrapping introduces never reaches
          the clipboard. %>
      <code id="mcp-url"
            class="flex-1 truncate rounded-md bg-gray-100 px-3 py-2 font-mono text-sm text-gray-900">
        <%= @resource_url %>
      </code>
      <button type="button"
              onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById('mcp-url').textContent.trim())"
              class="rounded-md bg-white px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-inset ring-gray-300 hover:bg-gray-50">Copy</button>
    </div>
  <%- else %>
    <p class="mt-3 rounded-md bg-amber-50 p-3 text-sm text-amber-800 ring-1 ring-amber-200">
      This deployment has not been told its own public address, so there is nothing to
      paste yet. Whoever runs it needs to set <code class="font-mono">MCP_PUBLIC_BASE_URL</code>.
    </p>
  <%- end %>
  <%# The one place a product is named, and #326 deliberately left it alone. Everywhere else
      the copy says "your AI assistant", because naming a vendor makes a product that speaks
      an open protocol read as built for one client. Here the name *is* the instruction:
      "Settings, then Connectors" is a different sequence in each of these, and a reader
      given a generic word would be left hunting through menus.

      A list rather than a sentence, so a client added later is a line rather than a rewrite.

      Checked against each vendor's own help pages on 2026-09-24 (#637), and both lines had gone
      stale: Claude moved connectors from Settings to Customize, and ChatGPT now puts custom
      servers behind a Developer mode switch and calls them apps, added from Plugins. Both are
      set up on the web or desktop and then work from the phone -- adding one from a phone app
      is beta in Claude and absent in ChatGPT -- which is worth saying on an app used at the
      rack. These menus move; the date above is when they were last true. %>
  <dl class="mt-4 space-y-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
    <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-gray-900">Claude:</dt> <dd class="inline">Customize, then Connectors, then the + button.</dd></div>
    <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-gray-900">ChatGPT:</dt> <dd class="inline">Settings, then Security and login, and turn on Developer mode; then Plugins, then the + button. Paid plans only.</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500">
    Do this on a computer or in the browser. Once it is connected, it works from your
    assistant&rsquo;s phone app too.
  </p>

  <%# What to say once it is connected. A connected assistant on an empty account needs to be
      told the lifter's lifts and numbers, and a blank chat box is the next place a new lifter
      stops. The same first message /start offers, so the two pages agree. %>
  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Then try asking</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 rounded-md bg-gray-50 p-3 text-sm text-gray-700 ring-1 ring-gray-200">
    &ldquo;Write me a four-week block, three days a week, built around squat, bench and
    deadlift. I am coming back after six weeks off.&rdquo;
  </p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500">
    What it can and cannot do, and what is stored, is on
    <a href="/docs" class="font-medium text-lime-700 hover:text-lime-800">the connector page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Connected</h2>
  <%- if @connections.empty? %>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500">Nothing is connected yet.</p>
  <%- else %>
    <ul class="mt-3 divide-y divide-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white shadow ring-1 ring-gray-200">
      <%- @connections.each do |connection| %>
        <li class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 p-4">
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <p class="truncate text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900"><%= connection.name %></p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-500">
              Connected <%= connection.connected_at.strftime('%b %-d, %Y') %>
              <span class="mx-1">&middot;</span><%= connection.scopes.join(', ') %>
            </p>
          </div>
          <%# Revoking takes every grant this assistant holds, not the one row behind this
              button: leaving another live would let it mint a fresh token seconds after
              being told it could not. %>
          <form method="post" action="/connections/<%= connection.id %>">
            <%== csrf_tag("/connections/#{connection.id}") %>
            <button type="submit" class="rounded-md bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-red-700 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-inset ring-red-200 hover:bg-red-50">Disconnect</button>
          </form>
        </li>
      <%- end %>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">
      Disconnecting takes effect at once. Anything the assistant already wrote stays;
      it simply cannot read or write any more without being connected again.
    </p>
  <%- end %>
</div>
